HASTE — WIND TRAIL EFFECT
Still source image for frame 1 of the approved 12-frame loop

REFERENCE IMAGE INPUT

No reference image is attached. Do not use the HASTE loadout card as a
reference: it is an opaque full-scene illustration, not a battlefield effect
sprite. Create an original, isolated magical movement effect using only the
approved gold-and-turquoise HASTE direction below.

PROMPT

Create exactly one still 2D fantasy-game VFX sprite: a calm instant of
gold-and-turquoise wind ribbons that will be the first frame of a subtle,
looping HASTE animation behind a moving allied unit. Render only the magical
effect; the unit, its feet, ground, terrain, projectiles, and battlefield are
absent because the game will composite this transparent sprite around a live
unit.

Use several slender, graceful, translucent wind trails sweeping horizontally
from a small, soft glow near the lower-center gameplay anchor. Keep the
brightest strokes and glow beneath and behind the future unit silhouette; the
central area where the unit will be drawn stays mostly transparent and
unobstructed. Let the gold and turquoise ribbons remain distinct at small
battlefield scale, with restrained painterly light and clean silhouettes.
The effect should suggest quick, light movement rather than an attack,
explosion, or impact. Keep the composition simple and balanced so the renderer
can mirror it for units moving in the opposite direction.

This is one still source frame, not a depiction of the animation's entire
motion. Make the ribbons feel poised to flow smoothly in a short loop, without
hard breaks, long motion-blur streaks, or a frozen burst. Keep the visual
weight low so the unit remains the focal point.

TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS

- Output exactly one PNG at 1024 x 576 pixels, landscape 16:9, RGBA with
  genuine alpha transparency.
- Use a fully transparent background, not a checkerboard or a dark/colored
  matte. Only the wind ribbons and restrained glow may contain visible pixels.
- Keep the full effect inside the canvas with a modest transparent safety
  margin; do not clip soft glow or ribbon tips.
- Preserve clean, soft alpha edges without a black, white, or colored fringe.
- No animation, sprite sheet, alternate takes, contact sheet, or variations.
- Save the source as `assets_src/spells/haste/wind-first-frame.png`.

